<title>CANADA: CBRS Reaffirms Ontario long and short-term ratings.</title>
<headline>CBRS Reaffirms Ontario long and short-term ratings.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Bond Rating Service said on Thursday it reaffirmed the province of Ontario's and Ontario Hydro's long- and short-term debt ratings at AA and A-1+ respectively, with a stable outlook.</p>
<p>The bond rating agency said it was unclear how the province would deal with Ontario Hydro's debt and how provincially owned Ontario Hydro would defend against competition.</p>
<p>Ontario Hydro said on Wednesday that it would overhaul its nuclear operations and suspend seven nuclear units at a cost of C$5 billion to C$8 billion between 1997 and 2001.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
